{
  "protocol": {
    "scope": "Post-hoc on four previously examined PINNS sites and eight frozen seed-42 networks. Descriptive trajectory-implied events; M0/M1 have no trained action head.",
    "targets": "Use five historical ground points and 30 true future positions in the official compute_action_labels rule (default speed/angle scales, 10 Hz). All windows complete. Start/stop can coexist with a turn.",
    "predictions": "Apply exactly the same rule to the observed history plus each predicted future. For M0/M1 sum the probabilities of the six modes that imply each event. The two constant-velocity forecasts have binary scores, giving their precision-recall curves fewer thresholds than the neural mixtures. No true future is passed into forecasting or scoring the modes. No tuning, fitting, or threshold selection.",
    "metrics": "Use a fixed >=0.5 threshold per event. AP is non-interpolated, grouping all tied scores at each unique threshold. Absent true positives make a class F1/AP null and exclude it from the class macro, while its confusion counts remain. Equal-site averages weight the four within-site class-macro metrics equally; pooled metrics instead concatenate all windows."
  },
